      "why": "The worst case, and the most ordinary one. Every call carries the same locale enum and the same key names, and the server's body repeats them verbatim, so a 16-byte run of shared field structure exists in every pair before a single word of the payload is compared. This is the family that makes the case for weighting a k-gram by how common it is."
